  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The verb and the noun for a breach share the idea of an opening. The beka’s value is explicit in Exodus. A stone weight inscribed bqʿ in ancient Hebrew script was reported by the Israel Nature and Parks Authority in 2018 from the Emek Tzurim sifting project. The derivation of the word for a plain from the verb ‘split’ is less secure. Arabic buqʿa names a distinct piece of ground without specifying its elevation."
